<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: every new function docstring names the section/figure it implements (Oster-Murray-Maini 1985 Sec. 4 for the progress zone, Oster-Murray-Harris 1983 Sec. 5 for anisotropy, Raspopovic 2014 Fig. 2E / Supp. 1.2 for the BSW Jacobian, Hall & Miyake 2000 for kappa_S, Saunders 1948 for ablation) and the Lean theorem it is checked by; laws 4-5 are registered with code and Lean loci in `oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.yaml` and the stale loci of laws 1-3 were corrected. Deductions: the diffuse-competence/prestress-balance formulation (L566) and the progress-zone noise term (L579) are modelling choices argued in the docstring, not steps of the source (-4); peak-detection thresholds (height 1.15, prominence 0.25, onset 0.30; L377-409, L590) and the 0.15 / 0.18 constants are uncited (-4); the Lean theorems formalise monotonicity and sign conditions, not the PDE dynamics (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py L377–L409: count_transverse_condensations thresholds (height 1.15, prominence 0.25) are uncited heuristics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py#L377-L409>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: the analytic marginal-stability curve and tau_c (L192-237) match the linearised Oster-Murray-Maini balance; the new 2D solver (L427-628) couples cell conservation with biharmonic diffusion, traction-driven drift and Kelvin-Voigt ECM relaxation to a moving free-boundary AER with a progress zone, which is the mechanism Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) Sec. 4 describe; the hybrid 4x4 Jacobian (L717-759) is a correct linearisation of the stated coupled system and its analytic-kernel limit reproduces tau_c = 1.2776 (self-test L1645). Deductions: the drift kernel 1/(E k^2 + s + mu k^2) (L508; 1D L329) treats viscosity as stiffness, so the solvers' tau_c = 1.4397 differs by 12.7% from the analytic value the figure reports (-5); the ECM balance is component-wise Helmholtz with no shear/Poisson term, no ECM density rho equation and the paper's -div(n du/dt) advection is replaced by the traction-drift velocity (-4); ad hoc constants (relaxation 1/(mu + 0.15) L327/L572-573, cubic -0.18 (n - N_0)^3 L334/L580, aniso_y = 3.0 L444) are not from the source (-3); the v2 Panel C was a kinematic template, so part of the v2 fidelity credit was unearned and is not restored here (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py L1251–L1261: Measurement 14 discloses tau_c(solver) = 1.4397 vs analytic 1.2776 (12.7%) — the solver does not implement the analytic dispersion relation exactly <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py#L1251-L1261>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: 14 reference-anchored measurements (L1069-1262), 9 new: 2D hierarchies vs specimen [1, 2, 4] / [1, 2, 5] (RMSE 0), 2D zeugopod/autopod spacing ratio vs the specimen's 1.373, proximo-distal onset rank correlation (1.0), Saunders series RMSE vs [1, 1, 2, 3] (0), synergy ratio 0.240 vs null 1.0, factorial [0, 0, 0, 4], corr(S, B) = -0.988 vs Raspopovic's out-of-phase prediction, and the disclosed solver/analytic tau_c discrepancy. Deductions: measurement 2 (1D wavelength = lambda_c, CV = 0.0000, L1129-1137) is circular — the periodic domain is W = 4 lambda_c and the m = 4 cosine is seeded (L312-313) (-5); the synergy and factorial references are model-internal nulls/predictions, not literature values (-3); the Saunders expectation is a qualitative mapping of stages to segments, not digitised data (-2); no absolute length/time calibration (lambda_c in micrometres, outgrowth speed in micrometres per hour) against the specimen or chick data (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py L1129–L1137: Measurement 2: 1D autopod wavelength vs lambda_c is exact by construction (domain W = 4 lambda_c with seeded cosine at L312-313) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py#L1129-L1137>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-1d-2d-solver-drift-kernel-critical-traction-tau-c-solver-vs-analytic-tau-c-disclosed-discrepancy>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-2d-free-boundary-aer-outgrowth-pde-forelimb-hierarchy-stylopod-zeugopod-autopod-rmse-vs-specimen-1-2-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-2d-free-boundary-aer-outgrowth-pde-hindlimb-hierarchy-stylopod-zeugopod-autopod-rmse-vs-specimen-1-2-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-2d-free-boundary-pde-zeugopod-autopod-inter-element-spacing-ratio-vs-salamander-forelimb-specimen>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-2x2-factorial-synergy-test-at-tau-0-85-condensation-counts-mechanics-only-bsw-only-sox9-feedback-only-hybrid-rmse-vs-0-0-0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-critical-cell-traction-bifurcation-threshold-tau-c-vs-subcritical-negative-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-hybrid-mechanochemical-bsw-critical-traction-tau-c-hybrid-tau-c-mechanics-only-solver-kernel-synergy-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-hybrid-model-sox9-bmp-anti-phase-correlation-corr-s-b-at-digit-condensations>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-proximo-distal-condensation-onset-ordering-behind-the-aer-front-spearman-rho-of-zone-rank-vs-onset-time>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-proximo-distal-limb-branching-hierarchy-mode-progression-subcritical-stylopod-zeugopod-4-digit-5-digit-autopod-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-salamander-forelimb-specimen-oedipina-ecuatoriana-autopod-inter-digital-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-salamander-hindlimb-specimen-oedipina-ecuatoriana-autopod-inter-digital-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-saunders-1948-aer-ablation-truncation-series-proximo-distal-segments-formed-vs-ablation-time-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-measurement-simulated-urodele-forelimb-autopod-m-4-condensation-wavelength-vs-analytical-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 remediation-round evaluation of `1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py` (87.1/100, down from 90.7 in Pass 2 although the model is substantially more faithful). Both v2 remediation items were closed: the kinematic 2D template that v2 had credited as a solver is replaced by a genuine 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (`_simulate_2d_aer_free_boundary_outgrowth`, L427-628) that produces the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, lays them down in proximo-distal order (onset 30.0 < 56.5 < 78.5) and reproduces the Saunders (1948) AER-ablation truncation series [1, 1, 2, 3]; and the mechanics are hybridised with Raspopovic (2014) Bmp-Sox9-Wnt kinetics (`hybrid_mechanochemical_bsw_jacobian`, L717-759; `simulate_1d_hybrid_mechanochemical_bsw`, L816-902) showing a synergy window (tau_c 1.44 -> 0.35) and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85 with corr(S, B) = -0.988. The same work exposed that the solvers' drift kernel is 12.7% off the analytic threshold, that the 1D wavelength validation is tautological, that the reference JSON's canonical parameters were never the script's, and that in 2D the autopod count is partly inherited by bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c; these drive the lower, more honest scores. 9 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (6 new, 0 sorrys) and 14 reference-anchored measurements (9 new). Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py at d58a084, image/png, 975928 B, 2604×2268 px, artifact_sha256 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff (sha256 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff), spec_fingerprint 176fd41f0d953b7b1e5e1437961112bdacb6e1e1e0faf2536dab887008a3d35d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 176fd41f0d953b7b1e5e1437961112bdacb6e1e1e0faf2536dab887008a3d35d; artifact_sha256: 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json=f2c0be56cbef12c2..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg=8030c8291c3a6d5b..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/scout_manifest.json=cb9d73c33c4113e4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system; the AER maintains a distal recruitment/progress zone and condensations are laid down proximo-distally | Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod) and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders) | Saunders (1948): removing the chick-wing AER at progressively later stages leaves progressively more distal skeletal parts (proximo-distal sequence of origin) | Raspopovic et al. (2014): a Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing network with Sox9 out of phase with Bmp and Wnt patterns the digits; reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with analytic tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9597 (lambda_c = 6.5472) and the 1D spectral-pseudospectral cell-ECM solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] on periodic domains W = m lambda_c with seeded m-cosine perturbations | A 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (progress-zone traction suppression and proliferation, AER regression, anisotropic PD cell diffusion a_y = 3, ectoderm-balanced prestress) producing the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, with proximo-distal onset order and the Saunders (1948) ablation series [1, 1, 2, 3] | A 4x4 hybrid Jacobian and 1D hybrid PDE coupling the mechanics to Raspopovic (2014) BSW kinetics (tau(1 + alpha_S S), +kappa_S (n - N_0)), with wavelength-matched ligand diffusivities, showing tau_c lowering 1.44 -> 0.35 and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85 | Morphological segmentation of the vendored Oedipina ecuatoriana specimen giving [1, 2, 4] / [1, 2, 5] hierarchies, autopod spacings 39.0 / 41.25 px and the zeugopod/autopod spacing ratio compared with the 2D PDE (1.235 vs 1.373); transfer_boundary: The 2D domain is a Fourier-periodic box with a diffuse (tanh) competence field, not a sharp Neumann boundary; the ECM force balance is reduced to a component-wise Helmholtz operator (no shear/Poisson coupling, no ECM density equation) and the viscous relaxation rate 1/(mu + 0.15) is ad hoc | The solvers' drift kernel includes mu k^2 in the quasi-static stiffness, so their effective tau_c (1.4397) is 12.7% above the analytic 1.2776 shown in Panels A/D; all supercritical regimes used exceed both | Only the proximal humeral/femoral nucleus is seeded in the 2D solver; the stylopod width W = 1.4 lambda_c is a tuned choice (W = 1.0 is marginal), and the autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c | The BSW parameters are copied from the Slot 016 reference JSON, rescaled in diffusivity to match lambda_c; the Saunders (1948) comparison is a qualitative stage-to-segment mapping, not digitised data; lengths are in lambda_c units with no micron calibration against the specimen; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element limb, explicit ECM density/advection, joint/phalangeal segmentation of the rods, Hoxd13 gene-dosage polydactyly scaling (Slot 017), or quantitative reproduction of the full Raspopovic (2014) 2D autopod (Slot 016)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:312-313 and :1129-1137 — measurement 2 (1D autopod wavelength = lambda_c, CV = 0.0000) is exact by construction because the periodic domain is W = 4 lambda_c and the m = 4 cosine is seeded. Replace it with a noise-only 1D run on a long domain (W >= 12 lambda_c) and report the emergent dominant wavelength and its error against lambda_c.",
        "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:329 and :508 — the drift kernel i k sigma_hat / (E k^2 + s + mu k^2) places the viscous term in the quasi-static stiffness, so the 1D and 2D solvers' effective threshold is tau_c = 1.4397 while Panels A/D, measurement 1 and the Lean law report the analytic 1.2776 (measurement 14, L1251-1261). Either solve the Kelvin-Voigt balance properly (mu k^2 du/dt + (E k^2 + s) u = i k sigma_hat and advect cells with du/dt) or re-derive and display the solver's own marginal curve.",
        "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:444-446 and :517-523 — the 2D autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation of the zeugopod rods (W_autopod = 3.0 ... 4.5 lambda_c all gave 4 rods during tuning) and the stylopod only condenses for W_stylopod in roughly [1.3, 1.5] lambda_c, so the 2D dynamics does not follow the m = round(W / lambda_c) staircase that Panel D draws. Add a shipped W_autopod sweep (3.0 ... 6.0) and a W_stylopod sweep as measurements, and overlay the 2D staircase on Panel D.",
        "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:566 and :579 — the ectoderm-balanced prestress sigma_drive = chi (1 - g_pz) [sigma_cell(n) - sigma_cell(N_0)] and the progress-zone mitotic noise are modelling choices that remove a boundary-rim artefact; add an ablation (bare penalised mask, no noise) as a measurement so the dependence of the 1 -> 2 -> 4 result on these choices is quantified rather than argued in the docstring.",
        "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:674-686 — BSW_PARAMS are copied from datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json rather than read from it with its SHA-256; read the Slot 016 fixture at runtime (verify its digest) so the hybrid inherits its provenance, and add a micron/hour calibration of lambda_c and v_AER against the specimen scale and chick outgrowth rates.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json:102-115 vs :116-137 — `canonical_parameters` (D_1 = 0.08, D_2 = 0.0025, s = 0.5, r = 0.2, tau_stylopod = 1.48) were never the script's values; the new `script_default_parameters` block discloses this. Reconcile: either adopt the vendored values in the script (re-deriving tau_c, lambda_c) or trace each script default to a source and retire the stale block; then SHA-256-pin the reference JSON." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.71e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: v_AER, t_ablate, bsw_gain, coupling and digits are CLI flags (L1682-1692, --sweep-2d); the ablation time controls the truncation level monotonically ([1, 1, 2, 3], Spearman rho = 0.95, Panel H); the coupling strength lowers tau_c monotonically along an 11-point curve (L928-929, inset of Panel I; self-test L1647-1648); autopod_digits = 4 / 5 sets the distal paddle width and yields 4 / 5 digits; the phase diagram marks the 2D-PDE zone counts. Deductions: during tuning W_autopod = 3.0 ... 4.5 lambda_c all produced 4 rods, i.e. in the 2D solver the digit count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation and is not the m = round(W / lambda_c) staircase of Law 3 that Panel D draws — this sweep is not in the shipped script and the discrepancy is not displayed (-7); W_stylopod = 1.0 gives no condensation and 1.3-1.5 give one, so the stylopod regime is narrow and tuned (-4); aniso_y, d_pz and gate_w are fixed and unswept although they decide rod orientation (isotropic diffusion gives stripes parallel to the front) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py L444–L451: aniso_y = 3.0, w_stylopod = 1.4, w_zeugopod = 2.0 fixed defaults; no shipped W-sweep of the 2D mode staircase <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py#L444-L451>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: deterministic seeds everywhere (seed + 100 * autopod_digits in 2D, seed + m in 1D and hybrid); the self-test (L1591-1675) checks bitwise determinism of the 1D, 2D and hybrid solvers, the analytic/solver tau_c relation, the synergy window, the factorial, the hierarchies, the onset order and the ablation series and runs in ~31 s; the memoising wrapper (L412-424) makes figure, GIF, measurement hook and self-test share one run per configuration; default render 31-60 s; CLI flags documented in argparse. Deductions: no requirements lock file for this slot and the environment is recorded only in this audit (-4); the matplotlib font-cache directory must be writable or MPLCONFIGDIR set, which the script does not mention (-2); the memo cache keeps up to 24 snapshots per 2D configuration in memory (~3 MB each) without a documented bound (-2); the dataset README invocation notes do not list the new flags (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credits: 8 primary sources with DOIs in the docstring (L6-34), `paper_citations.bib` and the reference JSON `sources`; the specimen JPG and scout manifest are SHA-256-pinned at runtime (L128-158); the reference JSON now records the script's actual defaults, the AER/ablation table and the BSW coupling table with their sources; the BSW parameters cite the Slot 016 reference JSON they were copied from (L674-686). Deductions: the reference JSON `canonical_parameters` (D_1 = 0.08 ...) still differ from the script's (D_1 = 0.28 ...) — disclosed side by side but not reconciled (-4); the reference JSON is hashed but not pinned, so edits are not fail-closed (-2); the BSW parameters are a copy rather than a hash-verified read of the Slot 016 fixture (-2); the Saunders (1948) table carries no digitised stage/truncation data (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
